zstd — third-party attribution

This file carries a CONDITION. The encoder in `src/` is a translation of C
source from libzstd (github.com/facebook/zstd, tag v1.5.7, commit
f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99) into Zig. The BSD licence that source
is offered under requires its copyright notice, conditions and disclaimer to
travel with redistributions of the source and to be reproduced with binary
redistributions. They are reproduced in full below. The obligation lives here,
beside the code that owes it; the root NOTICE does not list modules.

**Copyleft:** NONE-SHIPPED — libzstd is dual-licensed "BSD-style OR GPLv2" at
the recipient's option. This port is taken under the BSD licence only; no text
of this module is offered under, or relies on, the GPLv2.

WHAT WAS TAKEN

Translated (source, restructured into Zig but decision-for-decision the same):

  lib/compress/zstd_fast.c            no-dictionary `fast` match finder     -> src/match.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_double_fast.c     no-dictionary `dfast` match finder    -> src/match.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_lazy.c            no-dictionary hash-chain, row and
                                      binary-tree (DUBT) match finders,
                                      greedy/lazy/lazy2/btlazy2 parser      -> src/lazy.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_opt.c             no-dictionary binary-tree match
                                      finder, price model and optimal
                                      parser (btopt/btultra/btultra2), with
                                      its long-distance candidates          -> src/opt.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_ldm.c,            long-distance matching: gear rolling
  lib/compress/zstd_ldm_geartab.h     hash and its table, bucketed match
                                      table, sequence generation            -> src/ldm.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h  window helpers, hashes, ZSTD_count,
                                      seqStore, repcode handling            -> src/match.zig, src/sequences.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_compress.c        one-shot frame/block driver, frame
                                      header, parameter adjustment, entropy
                                      glue for a block                      -> src/frame.zig, src/params.zig
                                      post-block splitter and its block
                                      size estimates                        -> src/blocksplit.zig
  lib/compress/clevels.h              level tables                          -> src/params.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_preSplit.c        block pre-splitter                    -> src/presplit.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_compress_literals.c  literals section                  -> src/literals.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_compress_sequences.c encoding-type choice, table build,
                                      sequence bitstream                    -> src/sequences.zig
  lib/compress/huf_compress.c         Huffman tree, table header, streams   -> src/huf.zig
  lib/compress/fse_compress.c, lib/common/fse.h
                                      FSE normalisation, header, coding     -> src/fse.zig
  lib/common/bitstream.h              bit writer                            -> src/bitstream.zig
  lib/compress/hist.c                 byte histograms                       -> src/hist.zig
  lib/common/zstd_internal.h          code tables, default distributions    -> src/sequences.zig

Each of those files says so in its first line
(`SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause AND MIT`). `src/root.zig`, the tests
and `src/testdata/` are this collection's own work (MIT).

Not taken: libzstd's decoder (std has one), dictionaries, long-distance
matching, multithreading, streaming, `targetCBlockSize` super-blocks.

Run, not copied: `tools/` builds the same libzstd tag and runs it to produce
`src/testdata/goldens.zig` (lengths and SHA-256 digests of its output). No
libzstd bytes are stored in this repository.

